tempered (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * First release.  tempered presents a PCsensor TEMPerGold USB
    thermometer (3553:a001) as a Linux IIO device: tempered daemon reads
    the stick over hidraw and creates a virtual HID sensor through
    /dev/uhid, which the kernel's HID sensor drivers turn into an
    ordinary iio:deviceN, linked as /run/tempered/<label>.
  * udev starts tempered@hidrawN when the stick is plugged in and stops
    it when it is unplugged; the stick's keyboard interface is
    deauthorized so it cannot type readings into a console.
  * The last reading is held for 60 s (TEMPERED_HOLD) once the stick
    stops answering; after that the IIO device is removed, so readers
    see the failure rather than a stale value.
  * The daemon refuses to start if another HID temperature sensor
    exists: the kernel's hid-sensor-temperature cannot handle two.
  * tempered read, info and log (JSON Lines) read the stick directly,
    with the daemon stopped.
  * The tempered-hid library, MIT OR Apache-2.0, is on crates.io.

 -- Christopher Hoover <ch@murgatroid.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 20:48:33 -0700
